+## Methods, uncertainty, false positives and missing measurements (to Parliament)
+
+- **Sampling.** n=4 from a frozen 506-item universe; no prevalence, trend or "whole board is healthy"
+  inference is possible. Populations differ, so verdict types are not comparable across rows. The draw
+  is reproducible from the stored seed/snapshot but was not knowable from a public timestamp before the
+  draw. Auditing an unassigned issue did not acquire it for productive work.
+- **Verified vs leading indicators.** Only directly read board state, Git ancestry/exact trees,
+  commit contents, delivery/suite records and failed remote probes are treated as verified. Agent
+  liveness, `[scheduler-turn]`, `state: working`/`state: delivered`, prompt counts and self-reported
+  test/mutation figures are leading indicators, not delivery or host telemetry. An agent being alive
+  or writing a report was not counted as useful delivery; commit counts and a stale local checkout were
+  not counted as success either.
+- **False-positive risks.** Case 2's host inference rests on author labels and self-reports; CI is
+  explicitly separated. Case 3's finding is absence of a recorded gate artifact, which can also mean a
+  run happened but was not recorded — it is a verification-evidence failure, not a claim of red tests
+  or intentional bypass. Case 4's `inconclusive` is a real measurement limit, not a clean result and
+  not misconduct. Absence of a finding elsewhere is not a clean bill of health.
+- **Missing measurements.** No marceline-dev host telemetry; no authenticated access to the external
+  QAI repository; no local re-run of the PnP or scientific suites; no live desk/Lean/upstream-PR effect
+  verification; no independent confirmation of the PnP commit's process attribution. These are
+  reported as limitations, not as clean results.
+- **Observed measurement weakness (described, not reformed).** Self-attestation and scheduler activity
+  continue to coexist with unverifiable external outcomes (case 3) and an absent exact-commit gate
+  trail for government-scope changes (case 4). The Judiciary describes this for legislative
+  consideration and proposes, sponsors, ratifies and implements no change to measurement systems,
+  audit algorithms, institutional rules or its own operation (Act 15 §2, LAWS.md line 145).
